{
 "about": "Building style definitions for the B-1219 procedural building recipe (stage 2: styles as data). The engine side owns the generation mechanism; everything that makes a building read as one regional / period style lives here as data. A building spec names a style (\"style\": \"alpine\"); styles other than \"default\" are partial overrides, deep-merged over \"default\" at derive time (ai_loop/building_recipe.py), and unknown keys are rejected so typos surface. \"default\" reproduces the stage-1 recipe exactly (same constants, same seed derivation). Adding a style must never need a code change. Two sections: \"geometry\" is consumed by the CLI derivation (proportions, openings, roof, tints), \"materials\" by the Blender side (procedural material parameters). Tint-relative ramp shading factors inside the materials stay in code: they shade whatever tint the style picks, they do not define the style.",
